hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24177","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Mahmud ibn al-Rabi narrated to me, from Itban ibn Malik, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have become weak in my sight, and torrents come between me and my mosque, and I would love that you come and pray in my house a place I take as a mosque. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I will do, if Allah wills. He said: He passed by Abu Bakr and took him along, went with him, asked permission, entered upon me, and said while standing: Where do you want me to pray? I pointed to him where I wanted. He said: Then I detained him for khazirah we made for him. He said: The people of the valley, meaning the people of the house, heard, and gathered to him until the house filled. A man said: Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhshun, and perhaps he said Malik ibn al-Dukhayshin. A man said: That is a hypocrite man, he does not love Allah nor His messenger. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say; he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking with that the face of Allah. He said: O Messenger of Allah, as for us, we see his face and talk toward the hypocrites. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said also: Do not say; he says: There is no god but Allah, seeking with that the face of Allah. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No servant will come on the Day of Resurrection saying: There is no god but Allah, seeking with that the face of Allah, except he is forbidden to the Fire. Mahmud said: I narrated this hadith to a group among them Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, and he said: I do not think the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said what you said. He said: I swore if I return to Itban to ask him. I returned to him and found him an old man, his sight gone, and he is the imam of his people. I sat beside him and asked him about this hadith, and he narrated it to me as he narrated it to me the first time. Ma'mar said: al-Zuhri when he narrated this hadith would say: Then obligations and matters came down, we see the matter ended with them; whoever is able not to slacken, let him not slacken."
"24178","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Itban ibn Malik, then I met Itban ibn Malik and said: What hadith reached me from you? He said: So narrate to me. He said: There was in my sight something, so I sent to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I love that you come to my house and pray in it, and I take it as a prayer place. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and whoever willed of his companions. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in his house, while his companions were talking and mentioning the hypocrites and what they meet from them, attributing the greatness of that to Malik ibn al-Dukhayshin, wishing if the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated against him and evil befell him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Does he not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he says that and it is not in his heart. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, then the Fire feeds on him or the Fire touches him."
"24179","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Mahmud ibn al-Rabi narrated to me, from Itban ibn Malik, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said, then he mentioned similar. He said: Then I detained him for a khazirah of ours we made for him, and the people of the valley, meaning the people of the house, heard of him and gathered to him until the house filled. A man said: Where is Malik ibn al-Dukhshun, he said, and perhaps he said al-Dukhayshin."
"24180","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, from Itban ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in his house the forenoon supererogatory, and they stood behind him and prayed with his prayer."
